# Line-ending policy for the toolkit repository.
#
# Without this file Git normalises nothing (`core.autocrlf` is unset here and `false` on
# the maintainer's machine), so committed bytes are whatever the writing tool happened to
# emit. That drifted: before this policy the tree held 390 CRLF files, 534 LF files, and
# two files with both endings inside them.
#
# The cost is not cosmetic. A contributor running `core.autocrlf=true` materialises the
# tracked tree as CRLF at checkout; the next tool that writes LF then rewrites those
# files wholesale, and `git status` reports them as modified while each is byte-identical
# in meaning. `src/kairos_ontology/scaffold/gitattributes.template` records what that did
# to a real hub (issue #699): 168 files reported modified and `git checkout <branch>`
# refusing to switch. This repository ships that fix to every scaffolded hub and
# dataplatform while running without it -- this file closes that gap.
#
# LF everywhere, on every platform. Nothing in this repository is Windows-only text: it
# tracks no `.bat` or `.cmd`, and the one `.sh` would break under CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stated explicitly for the text this repository tracks, so the policy survives a future
# change to Git's `text=auto` heuristics.
*.py       text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.ttl      text eol=lf
*.rdf      text eol=lf
*.owl      text eol=lf
*.sql      text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.toml     text eol=lf
*.xml      text eol=lf
*.csv      text eol=lf
*.mmd      text eol=lf
*.jinja2   text eol=lf
*.template text eol=lf
*.example  text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.ps1      text eol=lf
*.cs       text eol=lf
*.csproj   text eol=lf

# Safety net. No binary is tracked today, but a fixture workbook or sample extract added
# later must never be line-ending converted -- that corrupts it silently.
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.xlsb    binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.zip     binary
*.pbix    binary
*.whl     binary
